.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Keeps track of all \fBIndex\fP objects once they have been registered\&. 

Serves \fBPropertyDatabase\fP to keep all existing \fBIndex\fP objects objects up to date, which is necessary when new variables are created at runtime\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
index tracking is necessary because some classes have indices as members\&. These objects can get invalidated when new variables of the same kind and place\&. are created\&. If so, for instance, the 5th scalar on the node might become the 10th\&.
.RE
.PP
By tracking all \fBIndex\fP objects that exist in a model, these can be updated by the \fBPropertyDatabase\fP everytime a variable is created or deleted\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
this implementation is based on the "Observer" design pattern\&.
.RE
.PP
